  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "Subnormal cell writes and *, /, ^ underflows flush to +0, while +, - and EXP(-745) keep subnormals",
  "statement": "Writing any positive or negative subnormal binary64 value or -0 to a cell via Range.Value2 stores +0 (0x0000000000000000), while normal extremes 2^-1022 (0x0010000000000000) and ±DBL_MAX (0x7fefffffffffffff) read back intact. In the 430 recorded bank rows with subnormal or maximum-finite cell arguments, all 179 subnormal-input rows read back as +0 and match the +0 control (SQRT(-5e-324) is 0, SIGN(±5e-324) is 0, ODD(±5e-324) is 1, EVEN(±5e-324) is 0, ISEVEN(±5e-324) is TRUE, ISODD(±5e-324) is FALSE, GESTEP(±5e-324) is 1, DELTA(±5e-324) is 1, and a subnormal divisor or significance in QUOTIENT, CEILING or FLOOR flushes to 0). Formula literals below 2.2250738585072014E-308 are refused at entry or parsed to 0. Products (*), quotients (/) and probed powers (^) that fall in the subnormal range flush to +0, whereas + and - retain subnormals and EXP(-745) holds 0x0000000000000001 in a formula cell. When fed a true computed subnormal x from EXP(-745), EXP(-730) or EXP(-709) (and 0-x for negative), ABS(±x) is x, SQRT(+x) is 2^-537, SQRT(-x) is #NUM!, EVEN(±x) is ±2, ODD(±x) is ±1, ISEVEN(±x) is TRUE, ISODD(±x) is FALSE, CEILING(+x,1) is 1, FLOOR(-x,1) is -1, QUOTIENT(±x,1) is 0, DELTA(x,0) is 0, DELTA(x,x) is 1, GESTEP(+x,0) is 1 and GESTEP(-x,0) is 0, while SIGN(+x) and INT(-x) transition inside the subnormal range (0 at 0x00000000001c7ea3 and ±1 at 0x0008bfe58468888d).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "430 bank rows replayed with Value2 input read-back and +0 controls, 22 subnormal bit-pattern cell-write probes, 16 literal-acceptance probes, 45 arithmetic underflow probes, and 180 true-subnormal function calls in Excel 16.0 build 20527 on 2026-11-08.",
